{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he set before them all these words</b> — the reason is that he said to them: Behold, I have placed the words before you, choose for yourselves this day whether you will do so. Therefore they answered him: <b>All that HaShem has spoken we will do</b> (Exodus 19:8), in the same sense as 'See, I have set before you this day life and good, death and evil' (Deuteronomy 30:15), and likewise 'And these are the judgments which you shall set before them' (Exodus 21:1) — meaning that they may choose and accept upon themselves to do them. And therefore Scripture says there (Exodus 24:3): 'And Moses came and told the people all the words of HaShem and all the judgments, and all the people answered with one voice and said: All the words which HaShem has spoken we will do.' And likewise 'And this is the Torah which Moses set before the children of Israel' (Deuteronomy 4:44) — meaning that he said to the generation coming into the land whether they would accept the Torah upon themselves, for he came to make a covenant with them in the plains of Moab as he had made with their fathers at Horeb.\\nAnd the Gaon Rav Saadia said that 'And he set before them' is like 'Put it in their mouths' (Deuteronomy 31:19), but it is nothing other than as I have explained. And likewise the meaning of 'And all the people answered together' is that Moses called the elders of the people, who are their sages and judges, for the choice is theirs, and he set before them all these words in the presence of the entire assembly, for concerning all of them he was commanded: 'Thus you shall say to the house of Jacob and tell the children of Israel' (Exodus 19:3). But they did not wait for counsel and deliberation, and all the people answered together and said, from the least to the greatest: All that HaShem has spoken we will do. And similarly Scripture says further (Exodus 24:3): 'And all the people answered with one voice and said.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:10:48.834710267Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}